#!/usr/bin/env node
// @typecheck strict
/**
 * Dutch for the admin dashboard scope labels (Nov 2026). Every admin section
 * now says whether it is about the whole server, one organisation (by name,
 * with the organisation picker for a platform admin), or the viewer's own
 * account (the scope bar in the dashboard shell), and three texts that
 * named the wrong scope were corrected:
 *   - the Look editor says the look is what everyone on this server sees;
 *   - the integration defaults are copied into organisations created in the
 *     admin and followed live by organisations without a list of their own
 *     (core/integrations/enabledIntegrations.js).
 * Also the labels of the dashboard's Organisation tab (its section groups, the
 * "choose an organisation" notice and the own-organisation-only notice), and
 * the n8n connection's notice that a new address needs its API key again.
 *
 * NL_TRANSLATIONS: keys this work added; written when a workspace does not
 * have them yet, so a workspace's own wording is kept.
 * NL_REWORDED: replaced only while a workspace still has the OLD shipped
 * Dutch (`was`), so an admin's own wording stays. The catalogues that shipped it
 * (hardcoded-integrations-agents-2026-10 and learn-content-2026-10, data files:
 * the lessons that named Settings > Organisation now name the admin dashboard)
 * are unchanged, so the boot ledger would not re-run them; the new Dutch
 * reaches existing and new installs from here. Idempotent. Auto-runs from server boot (boot/bootMigrations.js).
 * Manual:
 *   node server/migrations/update-nl-admin-scope-2026-11.js
 */

